<section id="flexibility" class="flex-sec">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Built for real life</p>
      <h2>An expensive week moves the date. <em>It doesn’t break the plan.</em></h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Most money apps treat one expensive week as a broken promise, and that’s usually where the
        saving ends. Lysning just recalculates. The dates shift to the honest new estimate, what’s
        free to spend adjusts, and tomorrow you start from where you actually are.
      </p>
      <ul class="tenets">
        <li><span>The plan flexes</span> — spend more one week, and the dates adjust instead of the plan collapsing.</li>
        <li><span>The date stays honest</span> — you always see the real arrival month, not the one you’re pretending is still true.</li>
        <li><span>There’s nothing to reset</span> — no streak to break, no starting over on Monday. Only a distance that keeps shrinking.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* An evergreen island: dark in both palettes, so it carries the on-evergreen tokens
     unconditionally rather than branching on the colour scheme. */
  .flex-sec {
    --accent-deep: #F0D4B0;
    --ink-inverse: #F0EDE8;
    --focus: var(--ink-inverse);
    background:
      radial-gradient(80% 60% at 15% 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 16%, transparent), transparent 60%),
      var(--island);
    color: var(--ink-inverse);
  }
  .flex-sec .eyebrow { color: var(--accent-deep); }
  .flex-sec h2 { color: var(--ink-inverse); max-width: 18ch; }
  .flex-sec h2 em { color: var(--accent-deep); }
  .inner { max-width: 64ch; }
  .lead { color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink-inverse) 82%, var(--island)); max-width: 60ch; }
  .tenets {
    list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: clamp(28px, 4vw, 40px) 0 0;
    display: grid; gap: 18px; max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .tenets li {
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink-inverse) 76%, var(--island));
    font-size: 1.05rem; padding-left: 20px; position: relative;
  }
  .tenets li::before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.7em; width: 8px; height: 1px;
    background: var(--accent-deep);
  }
  .tenets span { color: var(--ink-inverse); font-family: var(--font-brand); font-weight: 600; }
</style>
